{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## The file\n\n`src/rebar/signing.py` is **800 LOC against the 800 hard cap** — re-measured on `origin/main`\n@ `09abac96` (2026-08-19). ZERO headroom: any edit at all currently fails the CI module-size\ngate. (The original ticket said 798; the file grew by two lines between filing and execution,\nwhich is exactly the failure mode this ticket exists to end — Gerrit change 1916 failed today\nwhen a six-line comment pushed a 798-line file to 804.)\n\nDeferred from `cinderlike-lucky-akitainu` (which took `pass1.py` and `_store/push.py` instead)\nbecause this one cut cannot be made without editing a test, a different risk profile.\n\n## Concern map (re-measured on origin/main @ 09abac96)\n\n| concern | LOC | symbols |\n|---|---|---|\n| A manifest vocabulary + gate provenance | ~200 | `SigningError`, `parse_manifest`, `VERIFIED_AT_SHA_PREFIX`, `verified_at_sha_step`, `verified_at_sha_from_manifest`, `verified_at_sha_subject`, `REBAR_VERSION_PREFIX`, `rebar_version_step`, `rebar_version_from_manifest`, `_gate_source_dir`, `_baked_commit_sha`, `_gate_commit_sha`, `gate_code_version`, `head_sha` |\n| B legacy symmetric HMAC scheme | ~260 | `ALGORITHM`, `PAYLOAD_VERSION`, `_NO_KEY`, `signing_key`, `_generate_key_file`, `key_fingerprint`, `_canonical_payload`, `compute_signature`, `verify_record`, `_hmac_opcert_not_certified` |\n| C attestation dispatch + persistence + CLI arms (stays) | ~370 | `OPCERT_KINDS`, `verify_attestation_record`, `_sign_manifest_under_lock`, `sign_manifest`, `_resolve_and_reduce`, `most_recent_attestation`, `_record_for_kind`, `verify_signature`, `verify_attestations`, `sign_cli`, `verify_signature_cli` |\n\n## Design\n\nTwo cuts along the call-graph seams that already exist, producing **sibling modules, not a\npackage** (the cap is per-file either way, and `_opcert_signing.py` — split out of this same\nmodule in story 8d8e — is the established precedent):\n\n- `src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py` (concern A) — the vocabulary layer: the error type, manifest\n  validation, the two signed-manifest step vocabularies (`verified-at-sha:`, `rebar-version:`),\n  and the git/build provenance that produces the `rebar-version:` value. A pure leaf: stdlib\n  only, no rebar imports.\n- `src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py` (concern B) — the retired symmetric scheme, kept whole: key\n  custody, canonicalisation, `compute_signature`, and the `verify_record` verdict. Imports the\n  vocabulary layer only.\n- `src/rebar/signing.py` (concern C) — stays the entry module: scheme-dispatch\n  (`verify_attestation_record`), the op-cert sign path, the resolve/reduce read path, and the\n  two CLI arms. Re-exports the moved surface so `rebar.signing` remains the single import point.\n\nImport direction `signing -> _signing_hmac -> _signing_manifest`, acyclic; no back-edges.\n\n**The CLI arms are NOT cut** even though they are a genuine seam. A `_signing_cli.py` would be\n~105 LOC — above the 100 hard floor but below the 200-500 target band — and would buy headroom\n`signing.py` does not need: at ~370 it already sits mid-band with ~430 lines of margin. Recorded\nhere so the next person facing this file knows the cut is available and pre-analysed rather than\nre-deriving it. If it is ever taken, the CLI arms must reach `sign_manifest` / `verify_signature`\nthrough the module attribute (`from rebar import signing` in-function, then `signing.X(...)`),\nnever `from rebar.signing import X` at module level, or the eight `verify_signature` and one\n`sign_manifest` monkeypatches bind pre-patch and silently no-op.\n\n## The monkeypatch hazard — why this needs a test edit\n\n`_baked_commit_sha` is monkeypatched **on the `signing` module** at\n`tests/unit/test_attestation_signing.py:141,153,164`, and its only consumer `_gate_commit_sha`\ncalls it as a BARE GLOBAL (`signing.py:308,312`). Move both into `_signing_manifest.py` and\n`_gate_commit_sha` resolves `_baked_commit_sha` from `_signing_manifest.__dict__`, so a patch on\n`signing` becomes a NO-OP. Two of the three tests fail loudly. The third (`:164`,\n`assert \"STALEBAKED\" not in got`) passes **VACUOUSLY** — it silently stops testing the\nlive-over-baked precedence it was written to prove. That third one is the dangerous one.\n\n**Chosen remedy: (1) re-point the three patches at `rebar._signing_manifest`** — legitimate\nre-anchoring to the new structure, not a relaxed assertion; the symbol is private with zero\n`src/` consumers outside the family. Rejected: keeping the 69-LOC provenance sub-family in\n`signing.py` (splits one concern across two modules for no gain), and an in-function\n`from rebar.signing import _baked_commit_sha` back-edge (a cycle).\n\n**The vacuous-pass class is closed structurally, not by inspection.** A new guard test asserts\nPOSITIVELY that a patch on `_baked_commit_sha` is observed by `_gate_commit_sha`\n(`_gate_commit_sha(source_dir=<non-git dir>) == \"<sentinel>\"`). If the two ever land in\ndifferent modules again, that guard fails loudly instead of the precedence test going quiet.\nThe `:164` assertion is additionally strengthened from a negative (`\"STALEBAKED\" not in got`) to\na positive one pinning the live short SHA, so it cannot pass without the precedence holding.\n\n## Other constraints found (verified on this commit)\n\n- The re-export surface is measured, not guessed: 34 distinct `signing.<attr>` / `_signing.<attr>`\n  attribute uses plus 9 `from rebar.signing import` names across `src/`, `tests/`, `scripts/`.\n  EVERY moved symbol is re-exported from `signing.py` and listed in `__all__` (ruff F401 would\n  otherwise strip them, and `__all__` documents the contract).\n- `docs/reuse-surface.md` documents `sign_manifest`, `verify_signature`, `verify_attestations`,\n  `verify_record`, `head_sha`; `tests/unit/test_reuse_surface_doc.py` introspects NINE\n  `signing.*` callables with `inspect.signature`. Six of the nine move — the re-export must carry\n  them with unchanged parameter lists. That test is the CI tripwire.\n- Six PRIVATE names must be re-exported despite the underscore: `_gate_commit_sha` (imported by\n  `llm/build_drift.py:127`), `_baked_commit_sha`, `_NO_KEY`, `_generate_key_file`,\n  `_canonical_payload`, `_hmac_opcert_not_certified`.\n- **Silent-behaviour change to state in the commit:** `verify_record` and\n  `_hmac_opcert_not_certified` call `verified_at_sha_from_manifest` / `rebar_version_from_manifest`\n  as bare globals. After the cut those resolve in `_signing_hmac`'s globals, so a patch on\n  `signing` no longer reaches them. Audited: the one test that patches\n  `signing.verified_at_sha_from_manifest` (`test_plan_review_drift_floor.py:190`) also stubs\n  `signing.verify_signature`, so `verify_record` is never reached — no test depends on the old\n  resolution. The rule going forward: **patch a moved symbol in the module that DEFINES it.**\n- The 21 `rebar.signing.head_sha` monkeypatches are unaffected: every consumer reaches it through\n  the module attribute or an in-function `from rebar.signing import head_sha` (both resolve at\n  call time against the patched `signing.__dict__`), and `signing.py` itself no longer calls it.\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` has ZERO keys for `signing.py` — the ratchet is not a\n  constraint here. `.github/module-size-limit.txt` is NOT touched (it is locked; a contributor\n  change to it fails CI).\n\n## Portability\n\nNo CI-provider coupling. The module-size rule is enforced in-process by\n`tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` (via `tests/module_size_support.py`, the single source\nthe GitHub Actions gate also reads), so the constraint holds under any CI provider or none —\n`make test` alone catches a regression. Nothing added here triggers on a specific CI system.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `src/rebar/signing.py` <= 500 LOC with real headroom (target ~370, >= 200 lines of margin\n      below the 800 cap); every new module in [100, 500] and ideally [200, 500].\n- [ ] All nine `signing.*` callables in `test_reuse_surface_doc.py` reachable with UNCHANGED\n      parameter lists; the six private names re-exported; `docs/reuse-surface.md` unchanged\n      (the surface does not move).\n- [ ] The `_baked_commit_sha` hazard resolved by remedy (1), and the `:164` vacuous-pass risk\n      closed by a POSITIVE guard test rather than left latent.\n- [ ] Import graph acyclic: `signing -> _signing_hmac -> _signing_manifest`, no back-edges.\n- [ ] Full-suite test-count parity (no test silently dropped); `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n      and `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787177179404976001,"uuid":"4555c69e-8210-4bf6-9a9e-f3e160865a4c"}